The Ledger — Thursday

Cedar Capital closed a $400 million growth fund on Thursday, its fourth and
largest, the firm said in a statement.

The fund will write cheques of $15 million to $40 million into software
companies with more than $10 million of revenue. Cedar has backed 61 companies
since 2016, including three that have since gone public.

Managing partner Ines Duarte said the firm turned away roughly $150 million of
demand to keep the fund at its target size.

